WEBVTT

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:41.960
<i>Stay away!</i>

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:44.260
<i>No!</i>

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:06.820
<i>No!</i>

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:31.000
That was incredibly entertaining.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.090
Really?

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:50.850
<b>Goke,
Body
Snatcher
from
Hell</b>

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:36.720
I thought this might be to your liking.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.700
Yes. I was very impressed.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:45.840
I admire someone who can suck a human's 
blood without internal conflict or hesitation.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.840
He's a model vampire.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:49.600
I guess so.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:50.850
What's this?

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:53.540
<i>Crap. An annoying one found us.</i>

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.890
What are you doing watching a movie?

00:02:55.890 --> 00:03:01.330
Well, well, well. If it isn't 
Cinema Club Captain Maki Watabe.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:05.180
Such expository dialogue simply won't do.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:07.860
The scriptwriter really 
cheaped out this time.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:17.260
Who's this girl? Who is she to you?

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.450
Hey, wait.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.580
Very nice.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:22.420
You're used to being in front of a camera.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.310
By the way, this is 4K.

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:26.100
Skip the exposition!

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.130
Is she your friend?

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:30.590
Well, actually...

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:34.260
What's a pretty girl like her doing 
watching a movie with someone like you?

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.490
Someone like me? What does that mean?

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:39.780
I don't know who you are 
or where you're from,

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.830
but hanging out with this 
fujoshi is a waste of time.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:44.160
A worthless, trashy,

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:47.400
and mediocre triple-feature of 
rubbish that lasts all night long.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.800
I wouldn't do it if I were you.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:51.040
Rubbish?

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:54.870
If not rubbish, then trash. Water flea.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:59.340
An arthropod of subphylum crustacea, 
class branchiopoda, order cladocera.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:02.220
I'm a girl belonging to phylum chordata,

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:06.630
class mammalia, order primates, 
family hominidae!

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:09.230
But you're a blood donating 
enthusiast and a pervert.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:10.430
You're one to talk!

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:12.660
So, who is she?

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.860
She's a distant relative.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:15.650
A relative?

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:18.250
Yes, a very, very distant relative.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:19.390
She looks nothing like you.

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:23.860
She's my paternal cousin's brother-in-law's 
second wife's child from a previous relationship.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:26.860
I suppose I can go along with that.

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:29.520
Crap. If Mai's true identity is discovered,

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.790
it could interfere with our 
blood donating activities.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:33.710
You're really related?

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:38.500
I'm not sure exactly what's going on, 
but we're connected by blood.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.410
Anyway, I'm so hungry.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:43.870
<i>I need to get her home 
quickly and feed her blood.</i>

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:46.740
Then why don't the three of us go out 
for a luxurious dinner together?

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:47.550
What?

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:51.340
I know a nice place. I always stop there 
on the way back from the theater.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:05:01.030
<b>Gyoza General</b>

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:52.960
What? But, uh—

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.850
I'm hungry...

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:56.540
Then, it's decided. Let's go!

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:57.890
No, wait. We—

00:04:57.890 --> 00:04:59.500
Wait, Maki!

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:01.030
Come on, follow me.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:33.140
Handley Page Victor (B.1/B.2)
A strategic bomber used by the Royal Air Force (RAF) during the Cold War.
Developed by Handley Page Limited in accordance with Ministry of Aviation specification B36/46 under the name HP.80.
The crescent wings designed to reduce resistance during high-speed flight and T-shaped tail with dihedral angle give it a distinctive appearance.
Prototype WB771's first flight took place on December 24th, 1952.
Model entered service in April 1958.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:40.730
<b>6 Gyoza</b>

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:40.730
<b>6 Garlic Gyoza</b>

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:40.730
<b>Garlic Fried Rice</b>

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.480
Three orders of garlic 
gyoza with extra garlic.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:40.730
Three orders of garlic 
gyoza with extra garlic.

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.710
Could we also get three 
orders of garlic yakisoba

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.980
and three extra large orders 
of garlic fried rice?

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:50.000
Three orders of garlic yakisoba and three 
extra large orders of garlic fried rice.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.170
Got it.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:56.050
This place makes great gyoza, um...

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:57.870
I'm Mai.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:01.080
Mai-chan, do you like garlic?

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:05.990
<i>Crap. A vampire needs garlic like 
a cat needs currency—no, wait.</i>

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.010
<b>10K Ryo</b>

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.010
<b>Self-censored</b>

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:08.380
<i>Like a giant needs an iron club—no, wait.</i>

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.090
What about giants?

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:12.560
What? What about giants?

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.460
You know, sometimes everyone around 
you can hear what you're thinking.

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:19.730
Oh, uh... I sure hope that giant guy 
brings us our gyoza soon.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:22.700
So hungry...

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:24.830
Mai, are you okay?

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:27.650
It might be because of that movie.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:28.390
Huh?

00:06:28.390 --> 00:06:31.650
That movie would make anyone feel anemic.

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:34.780
Personally, I wish it had been bloodier.

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:36.490
I-I guess so.

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:38.660
Anyway, must be nice to be a vampire.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:42.490
They're handsome, popular, and immortal.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:46.340
That's what you call the superficial 
knowledge of an amateur.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:48.000
<i>This arrogant bitch.</i>

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.920
Who are you calling a bitch?

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:52.700
I sure could go for a 
bitchin' sweet dessert.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.870
In other words, your approach 
to viewing movies is shallow.

00:06:55.870 --> 00:07:00.140
Then why doesn't the cinema club captain share 
her thoughts with us since she's such an expert?

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.760
Thanks for waiting.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:05.390
Three servings of garlic 
gyoza with extra garlic.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:11.810
Vampires are only immortal 
in movies and novels.

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:15.510
But it's possible that 
vampires really do exist.

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:16.390
Crap.

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:17.800
What about crap?

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:19.780
Stop reacting to everything I think.

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:23.790
What real vampires have in common with 
fictional vampires is their need to suck blood.

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:26.420
Their sensitivity to UV light.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:30.230
The ability to modify their 
physical appearance.

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:33.260
Really? Then what about garlic?

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:35.760
You mean how vampires can't stand garlic?

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.470
That's fictional, as well.

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:41.220
By the way, their aversion to 
crosses is nonsense, as well.

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:45.560
So is their ability to transform 
into bats or wolves.

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:48.930
Real vampires are astoundingly long-lived,

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:53.280
but they age peacefully, 
and nobody can escape death.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:55.670
Exactly.

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:56.280
What?

00:07:56.470 --> 00:08:01.310
My stepmother Rubeus has deep 
laugh lines etched into her face.

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:04.400
Serves you right, bitch.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.680
Huh? Mai, what's gotten into you?

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:10.790
Gyoza rule.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.710
You ate all the gyoza?

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:14.020
At least put sauce on them!

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:17.140
You got a problem with me, huh?

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:19.820
Uh, oh. What's gotten into her?

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:22.770
<i>Is the garlic having this effect on her?</i>

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:25.440
Miss, please take your fight outside.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:28.980
Shut up! Stay out of this, phimosis dick!

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:31.350
The chef's got phimosis?

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:38.900
Where's our garlic yakisoba?

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:43.890
Where's our fried rice?

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.330
Mai, calm down.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.600
Good. Very good.

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:54.060
Look this way, my powerful lady.

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:56.500
Say butter.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:23.540
Girl consumes large quantities of 
gyoza and goes on a rampage!

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:23.540
Flying girl!?

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.870
<b>Mass Hallucination!? Drugs in the Gyoza?</b>

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:30.170
I doubt the police will take a 
story about a high school girl

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:34.420
demolishing a gyoza 
restaurant seriously.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:35.630
I'm sure it'll be fine.

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.040
You're probably right.

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:39.720
But she's not human.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:42.600
Don't feed her indiscriminately 
for your own entertainment.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:46.120
It's not like I fed her garlic for fun.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.800
I wasn't expecting garlic to 
produce that side effect.

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:52.990
Instead of being a weakness, it's like 
giving silver vine to cats or spinach to Popeye.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:56.100
Could Mai's reaction be idiosyncratic?

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:01.430
Unless we learn that vampire's traits, 
things could get even worse.

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:06.420
To prevent further damage, 
we should investigate.

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:13.550
<b>Test Number 1 / Mirrors</b>

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:18.790
Her reflection doesn't appear in mirrors.

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:24.220
<b>Test Number 2 / Photographs</b>

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:25.860
Say butter.

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:30.990
Phones can't capture photos of her, either.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:34.450
Wait, what? Didn't I just see 
her photo in the newspaper?

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:39.150
<b>Test Number 3 / Crosses</b>

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:43.060
How cute. May I keep this?

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:45.580
She's quite unconcerned by crosses, too.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:48.910
<b>Test Number 4 / Running Water</b>

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:55.290
She can easily leap over running water.

00:10:56.020 --> 00:11:00.040
Vampires aren't supposed to be 
able to cross running water.

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:07.780
It seems that vampire is different 
from the vampires I'm familiar with.

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:10.730
She's different from the ones I know, too.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:13.430
The vampires you know?

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:15.680
For reference, tell me what you know.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:22.310
Well... they're tall, pale, 
and wear black capes with red lining.

00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:26.660
They're nobles, live in castles, 
and are sometimes gay.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.610
They sleep in coffins during the day,

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:31.480
and at night they bite the 
necks of beautiful virgins

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:33.690
or plain old beautiful women 
and suck their blood.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:39.370
Their victims come back to life as vampires.

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:42.900
When their hearts are pierced by stakes, 
they scream and turn into ash.

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:46.010
Garlic, crosses, and the 
sun are their weaknesses.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:48.650
They sometimes transform into bats or wolves,

00:11:48.650 --> 00:11:51.330
and unless they're killed, 
they never grow old or die.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:53.210
What did you think of them?

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:56.150
Commonplace. Cliché.

00:11:56.720 --> 00:12:01.670
That's the product of a lowbrow 
filmmaker's sexual fantasies.

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:07.500
Like the author Bram Stoker's novel they 
based it off of, it's ridiculous nonsense.

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:12.460
But what about the vampire folklore 
that author based his novel on?

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:12.460
<b>Vampire Folklore</b>

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:16.380
They're muscular with reddish 
but dark and sinister faces.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.680
Most of them are peasants.

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:24.230
They rise from their graves and return home, 
where they bite their families or eat their food.

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:27.820
Additionally, they often transform 
into nocturnal creatures.

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:31.670
In other words,

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:37.420
they were inspired by scavengers 
who ate and lurked around fetid corpses.

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:44.600
A regional representation meant to rationalize 
the omnipresent phenomenon of death.

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:45.950
Therefore...

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:48.450
Listen to what I'm saying!

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:48.450
<b>SLAP SLAP SLAP</b>

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:52.000
You still haven't quit your corporal 
punishment and power harassment!

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.420
I don't give a shit about 
your power harassment!

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:57.530
Whether it's a sexual fantasy produced 
by the entertainment industry

00:12:57.530 --> 00:13:00.070
or a legend fabricated by a primitive people

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:03.690
with access to limited information trying 
to rationalize their world view,

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:07.990
they're still fictional. They don't exist.

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:13.850
And yet, a creature we could 
call a vampire does exist.

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:18.750
To be precise, perhaps we should 
call her a blood-sucking human.

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:20.480
She's a vampire.

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:23.850
What she has in common with 
those fictional creatures is...

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:26.470
First, she sucks blood.

00:13:26.830 --> 00:13:30.270
Second, she's sensitive to UV light.

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:35.190
Third, she can modify parts 
of her physical appearance.

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:37.350
Ow.

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:41.530
Regarding their immortality, 
we'll have to take that girl's word for it,

00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:46.000
but it sounds like while they are exceptionally 
long-lived, they're not immortal.

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:49.670
It's not like we can drive 
a stake through her heart.

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:54.560
Come to think of it, we haven't 
conducted the UV light test yet.

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:59.770
<b>Minamiguchi Fureai Dori Street</b>

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:59.780
Mai, how are you feeling? Any discomfort?

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:04.400
<b>Minamiguchi Fureai Dori Street</b>

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:03.870
My clan is quite resistant to UV light.

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:09.280
Though my stepmother Rubeus would 
instantly burn to a crisp.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:09.160
<b>Minamiguchi Fureai Dori Street</b>

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:13.330
I'm sure the worse a vampire's personality 
is, the more sensitive they are to UV light.

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:18.870
<i>Which means as long as she takes 
appropriate precautions against UV light...</i>

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:25.160
Wait. Hey, wait for me.

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:27.510
Hurry up.

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:37.510
<i>Well, it's not like I'm a man.</i>

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:38.100
<b>Mitsugu</b>

00:14:38.470 --> 00:14:40.280
What's this?

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:42.620
<i>It's Kaoru this time?</i>

00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:46.400
I wasn't expecting to find you 
cosplaying as an invisible woman.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:48.730
Not bad.

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:51.330
Well? Why don't we cosplay together?

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:52.500
Cosplay?

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:55.300
Never thought I'd see you here,

00:14:55.300 --> 00:14:59.390
Cosplay Club Captain and fellow 
Blood Donation Club member Kaoru.

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:02.930
Why are you speaking in such 
obviously expository dialogue?

00:15:02.930 --> 00:15:05.910
You've got the wrong idea, 
Kaoru. This girl is—

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:08.430
You wish to participate, as well?

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:11.470
Very well. I shall allow you to join us.

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:13.350
It's not like that.

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:16.640
<b>Cosplay Club</b>

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:23.970
You're quite cute, aren't you?

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:25.370
<i>She's right.</i>

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:29.250
<i>It may be standard, 
but it's extremely convincing.</i>

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:31.350
Let's try the next outfit.

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:46.750
<i>What a high-value development.</i>

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:48.460
What's high-value?

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:50.000
Oh, uh...

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:53.180
You sure do have a lot of 
high-value outfits lying around.

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:56.590
You know, sometimes everyone around 
you can hear what you're thinking.

00:15:56.590 --> 00:15:58.980
Don't repeat the same story development!

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:02.730
Instead of getting mad at me, 
why don't you try this on?

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:12.080
So niche.

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:14.820
I bet that's what you're into.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.260
You couldn't be more wrong.

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:18.220
I'm not a tokusatsu otaku.

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:21.560
What? You'd prefer a moon base catsuit?

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:23.330
I didn't say that!

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:24.690
Here.

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:25.830
What's this?

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:29.870
To tell you the truth, tonight we're 
holding our cosplay Halloween party.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:35.550
<b>Halloween Party</b>

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:31.600
A cosplay party?

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:35.540
That's right. It's hosted by the 
Cosplay Club and starts at 6 PM tonight.

00:16:35.540 --> 00:16:40.770
Since she'll be participating as a surprise 
guest, you should come with her.

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:40.770
<b>Halloween Party</b>

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:40.770
<b>Where: Akiba Cultures Zone
When: Starting 18:00 tonight</b>

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:45.380
A what? Who decided 
she'd be your surprise guest?

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:47.700
I made the decision just now.

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:51.160
I don't think that's a good idea.

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:53.570
I'll draw another 200 for you today.

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:54.820
Thank you.

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:56.740
No, wait. That has nothing to do with—

00:16:56.740 --> 00:17:00.100
We'll be waiting with a 
super cute outfit for her.

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:01.680
Here's your party ticket quota.

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:03.040
They're 2000 yen per person.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:04.540
You're welcome to pay for them yourself.

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:06.730
Anyway, thanks for handling those.

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:08.290
No, wait—

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:13.670
Now let's settle the 
Cosplay Club's accounts for the year!

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:13.940
Yeah!

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:16.800
<i>She really is a type B. She's not 
listening to anything I'm saying.</i>

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:15.170
Yeah!

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:16.360
Yeah!

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:44.460
Akiba Cultures Zone

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:49.570
Wh-What is this?

00:17:49.570 --> 00:17:52.110
Marvelous. You look amazing.

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:54.880
It matches your feel perfectly.

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:59.560
Mai, you don't have to do 
this if you don't want to.

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:01.860
I adore this outfit.

00:18:01.860 --> 00:18:04.890
I wish my stepmother could see me in this.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.000
I see, I see.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:09.220
Then let's show you off to your stepmother 
or stepfather or step-whoever else.

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:25.790
You'll be paying for this choreography.

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:26.960
Aye, sir.

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:33.990
I suppose filming stupid men in their 
natural state is a filmmaker's job, too.

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:36.770
Cameras two and three, 
make sure you don't miss this.

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:38.130
Huh?

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:48.750
Doctor Chihiro, what are you doing here?

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:51.090
I'm here for this.

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:54.880
I'm going to draw blood from these 
high blood pressure idiots.

00:18:59.020 --> 00:19:02.810
<i>Crap. This atmosphere doesn't look good.</i>

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:06.030
It's time for today's special guest.

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:23.670
Hey, brats!

00:19:23.670 --> 00:19:27.970
I won't let anyone lay 
a finger on my goddess!

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:27.980
Knuckle

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:30.930
Eat Hurricane Kick!

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:35.450
Don't think you'll get away with this!

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:37.120
Sorry, Jinko.

00:19:37.120 --> 00:19:41.820
Your ittokan tin can is fearsome, but our 
senior's fists are even more destructive.

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:44.150
Behave yourself.

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:49.020
That said, we'd be wasting 
our time if we stayed here.

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:52.890
And all three of us against just 
one of you would be rather dull.

00:19:52.890 --> 00:19:54.990
Only one of us needs to watch you.

00:19:54.990 --> 00:19:58.960
Rock, paper, scissors, shoot. Shoot.

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:05.390
Shoot. Shoot. Shoot.

00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:05.390
You idiots! Untie me this instant!

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:14.190
Mai, we're leaving.

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:16.050
What? Already?

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:18.190
I can't let you do that.

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:20.820
The event is just getting started.

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:23.780
Kaoru, don't you have any limits?

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:26.370
Limit is a word not found in my dictionary.

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:28.590
It's dangerous for us to stay any longer.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:33.380
You sex-crazed idiots! Are you ready to die?

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:35.510
Take this! And this!

00:20:35.510 --> 00:20:38.250
This isn't good. He's outnumbered.

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:41.250
The so-called Rising and Falling 
Battleship is sinking.

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:45.090
Okada, Kanbaru! Don't just watch, help me!

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:46.050
Osu!

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:49.980
Don't speak the word "osu" in my presence!

00:20:59.630 --> 00:21:02.470
Fools, this is farewell.

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:13.710
Now they've done it.

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:16.540
These effects are incredible. Are they CG?

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:18.580
They really put a lot of money 
and effort into this one.

00:21:18.580 --> 00:21:20.210
Where did they find the budget for this?

00:21:21.560 --> 00:21:23.420
Sir, are you alive?

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:26.230
My life is all I've got left.

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:27.590
He's gone.

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:30.470
He's not dead, you idiot!

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:32.630
Jinko, what are you doing here?

00:21:32.630 --> 00:21:33.900
Don't ask questions!

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:35.680
Jinko, wait...

00:21:36.430 --> 00:21:37.440
Shut up!

00:21:37.630 --> 00:21:40.390
I want to speak to whoever's 
responsible for this!

00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:43.610
All right. We got some good images.

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:45.540
But isn't this...

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:12.600
<b>Mass Hallucination at Cosplay Party!?</b>

00:22:12.720 --> 00:22:14.980
<b>Roof Collapses, Many Injured</b>

00:23:44.980 --> 00:24:00.000
<b>Episode 4 "Salamander's Night"</b>

00:23:45.740 --> 00:23:49.360
Come on. It's for scientific progress.

00:23:49.360 --> 00:23:52.830
Give me your blood!

00:23:55.160 --> 00:23:57.020
Delicious.
